1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
How many girls do you think have liked you without you ever realizing it?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,000
One, three.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,800
Maybe more than you think, and the funny part is, you probably didn't miss the girl.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,200
You missed the signals, because most people don't walk up and say,

5
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,400
Hey, I like you.

6
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:16,200
Instead, it usually starts with small things.

7
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:19,000
A look, a conversation, a little extra effort.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,800
And if you don't know what to look for, you can easily mistake flirting for normal friendliness.

9
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:25,300
So, let's make this simple.

10
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:28,600
There are three situations where you might notice these signs.

11
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:31,400
Number one, your acquaintances, you know each other.

12
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:35,200
Maybe you're in the same class, same college, same friend group.

13
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,800
But you don't really talk.

14
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,200
This is actually the hardest situation to read,

15
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:42,800
because you don't have enough interaction to know her normal behavior.

16
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:45,400
So, instead of looking for one magical sign,

17
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:49,200
look for repeated attention, eye contact, you look at her.

18
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:51,400
She looks back, you look away.

19
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,600
A few minutes later, it happens again.

20
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:56,000
Once, probably nothing, but if it keeps happening,

21
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,800
especially when there is no reason for her to look at you.

22
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,400
It's worth noticing, and here's the important part.

23
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:04,000
Don't stare back like you're trying to win a competition.

24
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,400
Just hold eye contact for a moment, smile naturally,

25
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,800
and continue what you were doing.

26
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:11,800
Her reaction tells you more than the first look.

27
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:13,800
She finds a reason to talk to you.

28
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:16,800
This is one of the most useful signs when you're barely acquainted.

29
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:18,600
She asks, what did the teachers say?

30
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:19,800
Did you finish the assignment?

31
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:21,000
Which one would you choose?

32
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,800
She could have asked someone else, but she chose you.

33
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:25,800
Again, one question means nothing.

34
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:29,800
But if she keeps creating small reasons to start conversations with you,

35
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:34,400
now there's a pattern and patterns are much more useful than individual signs.

36
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,400
She becomes more aware of you.

37
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:39,000
Maybe you walk into a room, and she notices,

38
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,400
maybe you're talking to someone, and she looks over.

39
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:44,600
Maybe you're leaving, and she suddenly starts talking to you.

40
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:46,800
These little moments don't prove attraction,

41
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,200
but they can show that you're on her radar,

42
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:51,400
and that's where you move to the second situation.

43
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,000
Number two, your friends.

44
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,600
Now things get much easier,

45
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,000
because you already talk.

46
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,800
You know each other's personality.

47
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:00,200
So you can compare how she behaves with you,

48
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:02,800
versus how she behaves with everyone else.

49
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:05,800
And this is where some of the strongest signs appear.

50
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,200
She mirrors you.

51
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,600
You change your posture.

52
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:09,800
She does something similar.

53
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,000
You lean closer.

54
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,000
A little later, she does the same.

55
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,800
You use a certain expression.

56
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,200
She starts using it too.

57
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:17,800
This is called mirror ring.

58
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:21,800
People naturally copy small behaviors of people they feel connected to.

59
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,800
But don't turn this into a test.

60
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,400
Don't start moving your arms around like a robot

61
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,800
to see if she copies you.

62
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:31,000
Just notice whether it happens naturally over time.

63
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,200
She tries to look her best around you.

64
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,800
This one is subtle, maybe she fixes her hair.

65
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:38,600
Adjusts her clothes, checks her appearance,

66
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:41,800
or becomes more aware of how she looks when you approach.

67
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,000
But here's the problem.

68
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,400
People groom themselves for many reasons.

69
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,200
So this alone means nothing.

70
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:50,000
The interesting part is when you notice it specifically

71
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,800
around you repeatedly.

72
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,400
Number three, texting.

73
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:56,400
Now this is where people completely lose their minds.

74
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:59,400
One message takes them three hours to analyze.

75
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:01,400
Why did she use this emoji?

76
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:04,600
Why did she say OK instead of OK, K, K?

77
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:07,800
Why did she reply after 11 minutes, relax?

78
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:10,000
You're not decoding a military message.

79
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,200
The biggest thing to look at is effort.

80
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,400
If you're always the one texting first,

81
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:16,200
always asking questions.

82
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:18,400
Always keeping the conversation alive.

83
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:20,000
That's important information.

84
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,000
But if she sometimes starts the conversation herself,

85
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,400
that's different, especially when

86
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:26,800
she doesn't actually need anything from you.

87
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:30,400
And finally, inside jokes, this one is underrated.

88
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:33,200
You have jokes that only the two of you understand.

89
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:35,600
A random word makes both of you laugh.

90
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:37,800
You bring up something that happened weeks ago,

91
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:40,200
and she immediately knows what you're talking about.

92
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:42,600
But here's the part most guys get wrong.

93
00:03:42,600 --> 00:03:45,400
You can find 10 signs that look like flirting

94
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:49,200
and still be wrong, because some people are naturally friendly.

95
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:51,200
Some people make a lot of eye contact.

96
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:53,200
Some people text everyone.

97
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,600
Some people touch their hair constantly.

98
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:58,200
So stop looking for one sign that says,

99
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:00,200
she definitely likes me.

100
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,200
Talk to her.

101
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,200
Get to know her.

102
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,200
And eventually, if the connection feels right,

103
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:06,200
be clear about your interest.

104
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:09,200
Because the goal isn't to become someone who can decode

105
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:11,200
every girl in the room.

106
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:14,200
The goal is to become confident enough that you don't need to.

